{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>For</b> — It is possible that 'I am forgotten from before HaShem' is because He does not save me, as though He forgot me, because he says afterward: 'For I heard an evil report' that they put out against me, so that all who hear will be terrified by it; or its meaning is, that I have terror from all around me." "<b>בהוסדם</b> — From the root סוד."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {0 "The comment addresses the word כי at the start of the verse; the quoted phrase 'I am forgotten from before HaShem' is from the first half of the same verse (Psalms 31:13 in Hebrew numbering)."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:29:05.806310141Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}